From: JellyBean47 <ebenjohn82@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ntdll: Name the time zone from macOS's /etc/localtime
 link.

get_system_config_tz_info only takes the zone name from /etc/localtime
when its real path starts with /usr/share/zoneinfo. On macOS the link
resolves into a versioned tzdata tree,
/private/var/db/timezone/tz/2026c.1.0/zoneinfo/Africa/Johannesburg, so
the name was never used. get_timezone_info then fell back to
find_reg_tz_info, which returns the first registry zone whose rules
match: every zone that shares its offset and DST rules with an
alphabetically earlier one is misnamed. Africa/Johannesburg became
"Kaliningrad Standard Time" (Europe/Kaliningrad to Chromium's Intl),
Europe/Berlin became Budapest's zone.

Take the name from whatever follows "/zoneinfo/" when the path is not
under default_tzinfo_dir. get_tz_info_from_zoneinfo_name still checks
that the zone file exists under TZDIR or /usr/share/zoneinfo and maps it
through Wine's "TZ Mapping" key, and get_timezone_info still discards
the result unless its rules match the current offset, so a wrong guess
falls back exactly as before.

Setting TZ instead is not a fix: msvcrt and ucrtbase parse it with
Windows syntax (tzn[+|-]hh[:mm]), and "Africa/Johannesburg" moved
Ubisoft Connect's log clock by an hour.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index dab9483..185dd6b 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -3080,9 +3080,15 @@ static BOOL get_system_config_tz_info( RTL_DYNAMIC_TIME_ZONE_INFORMATION *tzi, i
 
     if (!realpath( "/etc/localtime", path )) return FALSE;
     len = sizeof( default_tzinfo_dir ) - 1;
-    if (strncmp( path, default_tzinfo_dir, len )) return FALSE;
-    if (path[len] != '/') return FALSE;
-    return get_tz_info_from_zoneinfo_name( tzi, path + len + 1, year );
+    if (!strncmp( path, default_tzinfo_dir, len ) && path[len] == '/')
+        return get_tz_info_from_zoneinfo_name( tzi, path + len + 1, year );
+    /* macOS links /etc/localtime into a versioned tzdata tree, e.g.
+     * /private/var/db/timezone/tz/2026c.1.0/zoneinfo/Africa/Johannesburg,
+     * which never starts with default_tzinfo_dir. The zone name is what
+     * follows "/zoneinfo/". */
+    if ((str = strstr( path, "/zoneinfo/" )))
+        return get_tz_info_from_zoneinfo_name( tzi, str + strlen( "/zoneinfo/" ), year );
+    return FALSE;
 }
 
 static LONG64 get_current_tz_bias(void)
